---
code: K0002
title: Unexpected Character
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [ token ]
deprecated: false
---

The lexer encountered a character that is not valid in Kura source files.

Common causes include:
- Non-ASCII punctuation or smart quotes (e.g., `“` or `—`) pasted outside a string literal
- Unsupported symbolic operators not defined in Kura's grammar

Example of invalid source:

```kura
let count = 10 § 2;
```

Remove the unrecognized character or replace it with a valid Kura operator.

::: note
If you intended to use arbitrary Unicode text, place it inside double quotes (`"..."`). See the [EBNF](https://s0cks.github.io/kura) for valid lexical tokens.
:::
